      "time": "~35s",
      "narrative": "- Here we're looking at the code that connects our application to Foundry.\n- The setup is intentionally straightforward.\n- We establish a connection to our Foundry project, authenticate using our credentials, choose the model we want to use, and we're ready to start building agents.",
      "demo_actions": "Open the relevant code and configuration files in VS Code. Point out the Foundry project connection, authentication, model selection, and the minimal setup required to start building agents.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260622_142437_vlcsnap-2026-06-22-14h24m33s324.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~15s",
      "narrative": "- The real power comes from extending those agents with enterprise knowledge.",
      "demo_actions": "Set up the transition from base model wiring into connected enterprise data and tools.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "- Rather than relying only on the language model, we can connect to services like WorkIQ, FabricIQ, SharePoint, and Microsoft Teams.\n- Those integrations allow the agent to retrieve organizational knowledge and incorporate it into its reasoning, resulting in recommendations that are grounded in your business data rather than just the model's training.",
      "demo_actions": "Show the configured enterprise connections and tool access in VS Code. Call out WorkIQ, FabricIQ, SharePoint, and Teams as knowledge sources the agent can use during reasoning.",
      "screenshot": ".cutready/screenshots/20260622_142605_vlcsnap-2026-06-22-14h25m58s345.png"
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
