        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~15s",
      "narrative": "- As we're building, we don't have to leave Visual Studio Code to test any of this.",
      "demo_actions": "Transition from configuration into testing and inspection inside the editor.",
      "screenshot": null
    },
    {
      "locked": false,
      "locks": {
        "time": false,
        "narrative": false,
        "demo_actions": false,
        "screenshot": false,
        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "~40s",
      "narrative": "- The Foundry Toolkit gives us direct access to our hosted models, playgrounds, session history, traces, and evaluations.\n- I can interact with the agent, inspect how it's reasoning, review execution traces, and evaluate its performance, all from within the editor.",
      "demo_actions": "Open the Foundry Toolkit panels in VS Code. Show hosted models, playground access, session history, traces, and evaluations, then run a quick interaction and inspect the result.",
